msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Writing-A-Simple-Cpp-Service-And-Client.rst:245
msgid ""
"Next, the code waits for the service to appear. The ``while`` loop gives the "
"client 1 second to search for service nodes in the network. If it can't find "
"any, it will continue waiting. If the client is canceled (e.g. by you "
"entering ``Ctrl+C`` into the terminal), it will return an error log message "
"stating it was interrupted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Writing-A-Simple-Cpp-Service-And-Client.rst:250
msgid ""
"while (!client->wait_for_service(std::chrono::seconds(1))) {\n"
"  if (!rclcpp::ok()) {\n"
"    RCLCPP_ERROR(node->get_logger(), \"client interrupted while waiting for "
"service to appear.\");\n"
"    return 1;\n"
"  }\n"
"  RCLCPP_INFO(node->get_logger(), \"waiting for service to appear...\");\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Writing-A-Simple-Cpp-Service-And-Client.rst:260
msgid ""
"Next, the request is created. Its structure is defined by the ``.srv`` file "
"mentioned earlier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Writing-A-Simple-Cpp-Service-And-Client.rst:263
msgid ""
"auto request = std::make_shared<example_interfaces::srv::AddTwoInts::"
"Request>();\n"
"request->a = 41;\n"
"request->b = 1;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Writing-A-Simple-Cpp-Service-And-Client.rst:270
msgid ""
"Then the client sends its request, and the node spins until it receives its "
"response, or fails."
msgstr ""

